* Four-channel Darlington driver, written for the SimNodus examples (MIT).
* Like one half of a ULN2003: a 2.7 kOhm base resistor per input, open-collector
* outputs sinking up to 500 mA, flyback diodes from each output to COM.
* Copy this file into a model folder (Tools > Model Folders) to place
* DARLINGTON4 with Place > Subcircuit.
.model QDRV NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=150 VAF=100 RB=10)
.model DFLY D(IS=1e-12 RS=0.5)
* Pins: IN1 IN2 IN3 IN4 GND COM OUT4 OUT3 OUT2 OUT1 (inputs down the left side,
* outputs up the right side, as on the chip)
.subckt DARLINGTON4 IN1 IN2 IN3 IN4 GND COM OUT4 OUT3 OUT2 OUT1
RB1 IN1 B1 2.7k
RP1 IN1 GND 100k
Q1A OUT1 B1 E1 QDRV
Q1B OUT1 E1 GND QDRV
RE1 E1 GND 5k
D1 OUT1 COM DFLY
RB2 IN2 B2 2.7k
RP2 IN2 GND 100k
Q2A OUT2 B2 E2 QDRV
Q2B OUT2 E2 GND QDRV
RE2 E2 GND 5k
D2 OUT2 COM DFLY
RB3 IN3 B3 2.7k
RP3 IN3 GND 100k
Q3A OUT3 B3 E3 QDRV
Q3B OUT3 E3 GND QDRV
RE3 E3 GND 5k
D3 OUT3 COM DFLY
RB4 IN4 B4 2.7k
RP4 IN4 GND 100k
Q4A OUT4 B4 E4 QDRV
Q4B OUT4 E4 GND QDRV
RE4 E4 GND 5k
D4 OUT4 COM DFLY
.ends DARLINGTON4
